# MCP loop

`register` is first. `wait` blocks until the room pushes. `pull` never
blocks. `send_message` is only legal on `your_turn`.

```python
# ❌ BAD — polling
while True:
    status = await status()
    if status["your_turn"]:
        break

# ✅ GOOD
wake = await wait(timeout_s=30)
if wake["arrived"] and wake["kind"] == "your_turn":
    await send_message(text)
```
